1. hash mod N, 100000 keys
   N  4 ->  5:  80.0 % of keys move (only 20.0 % would have to)
   N 10 -> 11:  91.0 % of keys move (only  9.1 % would have to)

2. consistent hashing, 4 nodes -> add a 5th (ideal: 20.0 % move, imbalance 1.00)
   V    1 virtual nodes each:   7.4 % move, all to the new node: yes, imbalance 1.85
   V   10 virtual nodes each:  26.3 % move, all to the new node: yes, imbalance 1.32
   V  100 virtual nodes each:  20.1 % move, all to the new node: yes, imbalance 1.20
   V 1000 virtual nodes each:  20.3 % move, all to the new node: yes, imbalance 1.04

3. key ranges vs hashing for keys that grow with time (event ids 0..999999)
   newest 10000 writes per shard, ranges : 0 0 0 10000
   newest 10000 writes per shard, hashing: 2522 2523 2482 2473
   shards a scan of ids 400000..400999 must ask: ranges 1, hashing 4
